13. DynamoDB – LSI vs GSI

Using Amazon DynamoDB.

Local Secondary Index (LSI)
	•	Same partition key
	•	different sort key
	•	defined during table creation

Example:

PK = customer_id
SK = order_date

LSI:

SK = order_amount

Global Secondary Index (GSI)
	•	Different partition key
	•	can create after table creation

Example:

Main table:

PK = order_id

GSI:

PK = customer_id

Used for new query patterns.

14. DMS vs SCT

Tools:
	•	AWS Database Migration Service
	•	AWS Schema Conversion Tool

DMS

Migrates data.

Example:

RDS → Redshift

Supports:
	•	full load
	•	CDC replication

SCT

Converts schema.

Used when databases differ.

Example:

Oracle → PostgreSQL

When both used

SCT → convert schema
DMS → move data

15. Zero ETL

AWS introduced Zero ETL integration.

Example:

RDS Aurora → Redshift

Automatic replication without pipeline.

16. Databricks Lakehouse

Concept in Databricks.

Lakehouse combines:

Data Lake + Data Warehouse

Storage:

S3 / ADLS

Table types:

Managed table

Databricks controls storage.

External table

Data stored externally.

Example Table Operations

Table:

id | name | address

Operations:

Insert record 1
Insert record 2
Delete record 1

Backend in storage:

Files created:

part-0001.parquet
part-0002.parquet

Delete does not physically remove immediately.

Instead:

Delta log records operation.

17. Why Athena cannot update data

Athena queries files directly in S3.

It does not manage table transactions.

Therefore:

UPDATE
DELETE
MERGE

not supported (unless using Iceberg).

18. Delta Lake

Technology: Delta Lake

It provides ACID transactions on data lake.

Structure:

table_folder/
 ├── part-000.parquet
 ├── part-001.parquet
 └── _delta_log/
       ├── 000000.json
       ├── 000001.json

Data files

Parquet files with actual data.

Delta log

Transaction history:

insert
update
delete
schema changes

Supports:
	•	time travel
	•	rollback
	•	ACID transactions

